# Euler CRM regression guard

These rules are the ones recent fixes kept breaking. Check them before changing OEM sync, variant save, delivery, scheme, or pack price.

## Dealer body vs OEM invoice

- A variant saved in Euler sets `oemSkuConfirmed`. Later OEM sync and Mark Delivered leave that model, variant, body type, and price in place.
- The invoice body is stored on `oemBilledModel`, `oemBilledVariant`, and `oemBilledBodyType`. The drawer says which body OEM billed and which body was billed to the customer.
- A chassis nobody has confirmed still takes its own invoice body. One unit's body is never copied onto a sibling.
- A Coulson yard-body to invoice-body change (built FB, billed DV) still follows the invoice when the dealer has not confirmed a different body.
- Confirming a body is not an adoption. Do not run the Price Master reprice callback unless the working variant actually changed.
- Mark Delivered stamps the selected unit after the OEM patch is built. The final write must keep those delivery flags. Overlay names and labels onto the stamped units. Do not replace the unit list with the pre-stamp snapshot.
- Saving the current variant on a locked or delivered file still goes through the file lock. Showroom Admin cannot confirm a body on a delivered file.

## Price

- OEM billed date (`soldDate` on the unit, then the file) decides which list price applies — same order as scheme month. Booking date is only the fallback when nothing is billed yet.
- Coulson sync writes today's Turbo list into Price Master. For an OEM billed day before 1 Sep 2026, peel the ₹15,000 Turbo uplift only when that sync itself is on/after 1 Sep — an August sync already stored the August list.
- Opening Price Structure must not keep today's synced master on an August-billed file. A real booked figure that already matches the billed day (or is not today's sync) stays. A later pack unit without its own ex does not inherit Unit 1's header price.
- Pack rebuild prices each unit from its own OEM billed date. A September-billed extra unit on an August booking keeps the September list.
- Saving RTO or insurance on a booked pack unit must keep that unit's billed-day ex-showroom. A same-variant billed-day list correction must not clear Cx Demand. Preview and save use the same booked-price rule for every unit, not only Unit 1.
- ASM / RM field view does not get Price Structure or stored deal prices.
- A pack unit already paid in full keeps that payable when only the body name changes, including when Cx Demand was not already locked.
- An unpaid unit takes the new variant's Price Master price, and the previous Cx Demand does not stay on it.
- A lower RTO or insurance does not reduce Gross Vehicle Cost while a customer price is locked.
- A scheme amount changes the price only after someone selects that scheme.
- Turbo list uplift applies from 1 Sep 2026 only when Price Master has never been OEM-synced. Synced rows are the OEM invoice base.

## OEM sync

- Coulson sign-in posts to `https://coulson.eulerlogistics.com/api/v1/login` with Basic `username:SHA256(password):coulson` and an empty body. The typed password and the old `euler-auth` host are both refused.
- Chassis, invoice, and plate still come from Coulson for the chassis on the file.
- A different model family is not written on as a body change.
- After the whole file is delivered, the working variant stays until someone chooses Use billed body + price.
